  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Investing in Nature-based Solutions in the Pacific</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pacific Island countries face dire threats from climate change, for which they are poorly adapted in large part because they have pursued wasteful, inefficient, and environmentally damaging pathways to economic development. The program will enable Pacific Island countries to transform their economies away from the current inefficient and wasteful model, which is highly vulnerable to climate change and suffers from severe degradation of terrestrial and marine ecosystems, towards various forms of circular economies that are climate-adaptedative, suited to local needs and conditions, and reliant on nature-based solutions, efficient recycling of resources, and conservation of critical natural capital.</narrative>
  </description>
